NAME
       tput - ask about or control the terminal from a script

SYNOPSIS
       tput CAPABILITY

DESCRIPTION
       tput prints a terminal's property, or the control code that makes the
       terminal do something, looked up for the terminal in $TERM. Scripts use
       it to learn the window size or to clear the screen without knowing
       the terminal type.

       cols   The number of columns.

       lines  The number of lines.

       clear  Clear the screen.

       bold, sgr0
              Start bold text; return to normal text.

EXAMPLES
           echo "This terminal is $(tput cols) columns wide"

SEE ALSO
       clear(1), stty(1), tty(1)
